- ## coaxial, scintillate
+ ## coaxial, scintillate

- - `coaxial.streamsDuplex(in, out, negotiated)(shutdown)` is public: a `Duplex` over a blocking
-   `InputStream`/`OutputStream` pair, whose read side ends at EOF. scintillate's `Http2Serve.serve`
-   and `serveSession` take a `Tactic[Async.Error]` (for the connection's start), and the
-   per-stream daemons report their own faults. (#2328 follow-up)
- - `coaxial.Socket.Backend`'s `listenTcp(port, interface, options): ServerSocket` and
-   `listenDomain(address, options): ServerSocket` are `… raises Bind.Error`; its
-   `dialTcp(endpoint, interface, options): Exchange`, `dialTcpPort(port, interface, options):
-   Exchange`, `dialDomain(address, options): Exchange`, `duplexTcp(endpoint, interface,
-   options): Duplex` and `duplexDomain(address, options): Duplex` are `… raises Socket.Error`.
-   The JVM and Scala Native backends classify the `java.io.IOException` they threw before:
-   a bind failure as `Bind.Error(PortInUse | PermissionDenied | AddressUnavailable)` by the
-   JDK's message, and a connect failure as `Socket.Error(Dns | Refused | Timeout | Connect)`
-   (`Handshake` for a TLS failure); the native backend raises `Unsupported` for a Unix-domain
-   socket where before it threw `UnsupportedOperationException`. A user backend adds the
-   clauses and raises rather than throws. (#2350)
- - `coaxial.Socket.Error.Reason` gains `Connect` (6), `Refused` (7), `Dns` (8) and
-   `Unsupported` (9); `coaxial.Bind.Error.Reason` gains `Unsupported` (4). (#2350)
- - `coaxial.Bindable#bind(socket, interface): Binding` is `bind(socket, interface): Binding
-   raises Bind.Error`; `coaxial.Connectable#connect(endpoint, interface): Duplex` is `connect(…):
-   Duplex raises Socket.Error`; `coaxial.Routable#connect(endpoint, interface): Connection`
-   (which `Serviceable` extends) is `connect(…): Connection raises Socket.Error`. An instance
-   adds the clause. A `Connectable` can no longer be written as a lambda (a method with a
-   context-function result is not a single abstract method): an instance over a connection that
-   cannot fail to open is `Connectable((endpoint, interface) => duplex)` through the new
-   `Connectable.apply[self](lambda: (self, Optional[MacAddress]) -> Duplex): self is
-   Connectable`. (#2350)
- - The coaxial extensions `endpoint.transmit(input)`, `endpoint.duplex(lambda)`,
+ - `coaxial.streamsDuplex(in, out, negotiated)(shutdown)` es público: un `Duplex` sobre un par
+   bloqueante `InputStream`/`OutputStream`, cuyo lado de lectura termina en EOF. El
+   `Http2Serve.serve` y el `serveSession` de scintillate toman una `Tactic[Async.Error]` (para el
+   arranque de la conexión), y los demonios de cada flujo notifican sus propios fallos.
+   (continuación de #2328)
+ - Los métodos `listenTcp(port, interface, options): ServerSocket` y
+   `listenDomain(address, options): ServerSocket` de `coaxial.Socket.Backend` son
+   `… raises Bind.Error`; sus métodos `dialTcp(endpoint, interface, options): Exchange`,
+   `dialTcpPort(port, interface, options): Exchange`, `dialDomain(address, options): Exchange`,
+   `duplexTcp(endpoint, interface, options): Duplex` y `duplexDomain(address, options): Duplex`
+   son `… raises Socket.Error`. Los backends de la JVM y de Scala Native clasifican la
+   `java.io.IOException` que antes lanzaban: un fallo de enlace como
+   `Bind.Error(PortInUse | PermissionDenied | AddressUnavailable)` según el mensaje de la JDK, y
+   un fallo de conexión como `Socket.Error(Dns | Refused | Timeout | Connect)` (`Handshake` para
+   un fallo de TLS); el backend nativo lanza `Unsupported` para un socket de dominio Unix, cuando
+   antes lanzaba `UnsupportedOperationException`. Un backend de usuario añade las cláusulas y
+   lanza errores en lugar de excepciones. (#2350)
+ - `coaxial.Socket.Error.Reason` gana `Connect` (6), `Refused` (7), `Dns` (8) y
+   `Unsupported` (9); `coaxial.Bind.Error.Reason` gana `Unsupported` (4). (#2350)
+ - `coaxial.Bindable#bind(socket, interface): Binding` es
+   `bind(socket, interface): Binding raises Bind.Error`;
+   `coaxial.Connectable#connect(endpoint, interface): Duplex` es
+   `connect(…): Duplex raises Socket.Error`;
+   `coaxial.Routable#connect(endpoint, interface): Connection` (que `Serviceable` extiende) es
+   `connect(…): Connection raises Socket.Error`. Una instancia añade la cláusula. Un
+   `Connectable` ya no puede escribirse como lambda (un método con un resultado de función
+   contextual no es un único método abstracto): una instancia sobre una conexión que no puede
+   fallar al abrirse es `Connectable((endpoint, interface) => duplex)` mediante el nuevo
+   `Connectable.apply[self](lambda: (self, Optional[MacAddress]) -> Duplex): self is Connectable`.
+   (#2350)
+ - Las extensiones de coaxial `endpoint.transmit(input)`, `endpoint.duplex(lambda)`,

-   `endpoint.duplex(lambda)(interface)`, `endpoint.react(initial)(handle)`,
+   `endpoint.duplex(lambda)(interface)`, `endpoint.react(initial)(handle)`,

-   `endpoint.exchange(initial)(handle)(interact)` and the datagram `endpoint.transmit(message)`
-   take a `Tactic[Socket.Error]` (as a `using` parameter beside their existing ones), through
-   which a connection that could not be made is raised, where before the backend's exception
-   was thrown. `endpoint.listen`/`listenOn` are unchanged in signature: their declared
-   `Bind.Error` is now actually raised for a bind failure. The given
-   `coaxial.connectableSessional` likewise takes `socketError: Tactic[Socket.Error]`. (#2350)
- - `telekinesis.Http2.Endpoint#connect()` takes `socketError: Tactic[Socket.Error]` beside
-   `monitor`, `probate` and `asyncError`, and raises the socket's failure through it (before,
-   the failure cancelled the connection's readiness and surfaced as `Async.Error(Cancelled)`).
-   `Http2.EndpointSessional` and its given `Http2.sessional`, the given `Http2.Client.http2`,
-   `obligatory.GrpcSessional` and its given `Grpc.Endpoint.sessional`, `Grpc.Channel.apply`,
-   `embarcadero.Containerd.apply`, `perihelion.WsSessional` and its given `wsSessional`, and
-   `vivisection.Debugger.Sessional` and its given `Debugger.sessional` all take a
-   `socketError: Tactic[Socket.Error]` likewise. (#2350)
- - `telekinesis`'s socket-backed HTTP clients map a `Socket.Error` onto `Connect.Error` by reason
-   (`Dns`, `Refused`, `Timeout`, `Ssl(Handshake)`, else `Unknown`) where before they matched
-   the JDK exception's message; a TLS failure other than a handshake failure (a protocol, peer
-   or key failure) is now reported as `Ssl(Handshake)` rather than `Ssl(Protocol | Peer |
-   Key)`. (#2350)
- - `susurration.Ssh.Error.Reason` gains `Unreachable(reason: Socket.Error.Reason)` (14), raised
-   by `Ssh.Endpoint`'s session when the connection cannot be made, where before the socket's
-   exception was thrown; an agent socket that cannot be opened is `Reason.Agent`. (#2350)
+   `endpoint.exchange(initial)(handle)(interact)` y el `endpoint.transmit(message)` de
+   datagramas toman una `Tactic[Socket.Error]` (como parámetro `using` junto a los que ya
+   tenían), a través de la cual se lanza una conexión que no se pudo establecer, cuando antes se
+   lanzaba la excepción del backend. `endpoint.listen`/`listenOn` no cambian de signatura: su
+   `Bind.Error` declarado se lanza ahora de verdad ante un fallo de enlace. El given
+   `coaxial.connectableSessional` toma igualmente `socketError: Tactic[Socket.Error]`. (#2350)
+ - `telekinesis.Http2.Endpoint#connect()` toma `socketError: Tactic[Socket.Error]` junto a
+   `monitor`, `probate` y `asyncError`, y lanza a través de ella el fallo del socket (antes, el
+   fallo cancelaba la disponibilidad de la conexión y aparecía como `Async.Error(Cancelled)`).
+   `Http2.EndpointSessional` y su given `Http2.sessional`, el given `Http2.Client.http2`,
+   `obligatory.GrpcSessional` y su given `Grpc.Endpoint.sessional`, `Grpc.Channel.apply`,
+   `embarcadero.Containerd.apply`, `perihelion.WsSessional` y su given `wsSessional`, y
+   `vivisection.Debugger.Sessional` y su given `Debugger.sessional` toman todos igualmente un
+   `socketError: Tactic[Socket.Error]`. (#2350)
+ - Los clientes HTTP de `telekinesis` respaldados por sockets traducen un `Socket.Error` a
+   `Connect.Error` según el motivo (`Dns`, `Refused`, `Timeout`, `Ssl(Handshake)`, y si no
+   `Unknown`), cuando antes comparaban el mensaje de la excepción de la JDK; un fallo de TLS
+   distinto de un fallo de negociación (un fallo de protocolo, del par o de clave) se notifica
+   ahora como `Ssl(Handshake)` en lugar de `Ssl(Protocol | Peer | Key)`. (#2350)
+ - `susurration.Ssh.Error.Reason` gana `Unreachable(reason: Socket.Error.Reason)` (14), que lanza
+   la sesión de `Ssh.Endpoint` cuando no se puede establecer la conexión, cuando antes se lanzaba
+   la excepción del socket; un socket de agente que no se puede abrir es `Reason.Agent`. (#2350)

