- ## superlunary, sedentary, exoskeleton
+ ## superlunary, sedentary, exoskeleton

- - `superlunary.Rig#stage(path: Path on Linux): Target` and `Rig#invoke[output](stage:
-   Stage[output, Form, Target]): Result[output]` (abstract) are `stage(path: Path on
-   Linux)(using Tactic[Rig.Error]): Target` and `invoke[output](stage: Stage[output, Form,
-   Target])(using Tactic[Rig.Error]): Result[output]`; an implementation adds the clause and
-   raises a `Rig.Error` where before it threw. `Rig.Error.Reason` gains `Staging` (4: the
-   staged code could not be built or deployed) and `Invocation` (5: the staged code could not
-   be invoked), which the provided rigs (`superlunary.Jvm`, `superlunary.Isolation`,
-   `sedentary.Bench`, `Stress`, `Profile`, `exoskeleton.Enclave`) raise through `dispatch`'s
-   existing `raises Rig.Error` for a `Link.Error`, `Async.Error`, `Exec.Error`, `Bench.Error`
-   or `Name.Error` that was thrown before. (#2350)
+ - `superlunary.Rig#stage(path: Path on Linux): Target` y
+   `Rig#invoke[output](stage: Stage[output, Form, Target]): Result[output]` (abstractos) son
+   `stage(path: Path on Linux)(using Tactic[Rig.Error]): Target` e
+   `invoke[output](stage: Stage[output, Form, Target])(using Tactic[Rig.Error]): Result[output]`;
+   una implementación añade la cláusula y lanza un `Rig.Error` donde antes lanzaba una
+   excepción. `Rig.Error.Reason` gana `Staging` (4: el código por etapas no se pudo construir ni
+   desplegar) e `Invocation` (5: el código por etapas no se pudo invocar), que los montajes
+   proporcionados (`superlunary.Jvm`, `superlunary.Isolation`, `sedentary.Bench`, `Stress`,
+   `Profile`, `exoskeleton.Enclave`) lanzan a través del `raises Rig.Error` ya existente de
+   `dispatch` para un `Link.Error`, `Async.Error`, `Exec.Error`, `Bench.Error` o `Name.Error`
+   que antes se lanzaba como excepción. (#2350)

- ## aviation
+ ## aviation

- - `Monthstamp - day` (the `monthstampSubtraction` inline operator) is a compile error, naming
-   the operand, when its year, month or day is not a literal, or when the `RomanCalendar` in
-   scope is not one of `calendars.gregorianCalendar`, `julianCalendar`, `papalCutover` or
-   `britishCutover` (or a local `val`/`given` alias of one, which is followed to its
-   right-hand side); where before a non-literal date was checked at runtime and `Moment.Error`
-   thrown. A literal date is checked at expansion as before. A date computed at runtime is
-   built with the calendar's `jdn(year, month, day)` under a `Tactic[Moment.Error]`. The
-   witness `Monthstamp.monthstampSubtractable` (a pure `Subtractable`) is unchanged, and
-   panics (not raises) when `subtract` is called directly with a day the month does not have.
-   (#2350, #2372)
+ - `Monthstamp - day` (el operador inline `monthstampSubtraction`) es un error de compilación,
+   que nombra el operando, cuando su año, su mes o su día no es un literal, o cuando el
+   `RomanCalendar` que está en el ámbito no es uno de `calendars.gregorianCalendar`,
+   `julianCalendar`, `papalCutover` o `britishCutover` (o un alias local `val`/`given` de uno de
+   ellos, que se sigue hasta su lado derecho); antes, una fecha no literal se comprobaba en tiempo
+   de ejecución y se lanzaba `Moment.Error`. Una fecha literal se comprueba en la expansión, como
+   antes. Una fecha calculada en tiempo de ejecución se construye con el `jdn(year, month, day)`
+   del calendario con una `Tactic[Moment.Error]`. El testigo `Monthstamp.monthstampSubtractable`
+   (un `Subtractable` puro) no cambia, y provoca un pánico (no lanza un error) cuando se llama
+   directamente a `subtract` con un día que el mes no tiene. (#2350, #2372)

- ## polyvinyl, jacinta, xylophone, stratiform
+ ## polyvinyl, jacinta, xylophone, stratiform

- - `polyvinyl.Specification#fields: List[(Text, Member)]` (abstract) is `fields(using
-   Tactic[Specification.Error]): List[(Text, Member)]`, where `polyvinyl.Specification.Error(detail:
-   Message)(using Diagnostics)` is new: a schema which cannot be read is raised, and the
-   `record`/`tuple` macros halt with its message at the use site, where before the provider's
-   reading threw during expansion. An implementation adds the clause (a fixed list needs no
-   tactic). `Json.Provider#fields`, `Xml.Provider#fields` and `Tel.Provider#fields` follow, each
-   mitigating its format's errors (`Json.Error`; `Xsd.Error` and `Parse.Error`; `Tel.Error` and
-   `Tels.Resolution.Error`) into `Specification.Error`. (#2369)
- - `xylophone.Xml.Provider.Schema` is a trait, `def xsd(using Tactic[Specification.Error]): Xsd`,
-   where before it was `class Schema(val xsd: Xsd)`; its conversions from `Xsd`, `Xml`, `Text` and
-   any `Readable to Text` source are unchanged in use, but parse lazily, under that tactic.
-   `Xml.Provider#xsd: Xsd` (a `val`) is `def xsd(using Tactic[Specification.Error]): Xsd`; the
-   schema is read once, by the macro, and a provider whose schema never parsed panics at its
-   first runtime use. (#2369)
